  interpretation:
    * fresh/open slot:  18 choices, mix of expanding (depth+1)
      and one terminating (lit).  AI heuristic: near depth-
      budget, prefer terminating.
    * LET name slot:    1 choice only (lit).  Sharp constraint.
    * SEQ variadic:    19 choices incl. END (the terminator).
      Effects visible per-token: surprise / conserve / budget
      are flagged for AI's static reasoning.

==============================================================================
  L2 -- enriched anomaly reports (machine-actionable)
==============================================================================

  Scenario A: budget exceeded on a 5-node body under budget=3
    program: (budget Lit(3) (merge (p Lit(3)) (tau Lit(12))))
    trap raised: BUDGET trap: spent 4 > limit 3 (overrun 1)
    anomaly:
    kind:             'budget-exceeded'
    detail:           {'limit': 3, 'spent': 4, 'overrun': 1}
    position_path:    (16, 3, 9)  (opcode chain)
    offending_op:     0x09 (tau)
    valid_alts:       (8, 10, 15)  (['p', 'sigma', 'mobius'])
    repair_hint:      reduce body size (fewer operators) or raise budget to >= 4

  Scenario B: conservation violated (violate bumps value by +1)
    program: (conserve Lit(77) (violate Lit(77)))
    trap raised: Delta trap: conserve/equality violated -- entry 77 vs exit 78
    anomaly:
    kind:             'conservation-violated'
    detail:           {'invariant': 'conserve/equality', 'entry': 77, 'exit': 78, 'deviation': 1}
    position_path:    (17,)  (opcode chain)
    offending_op:     0x11 (conserve)
    valid_alts:       (none)
    repair_hint:      replace operator `conserve` with one of [] to keep the body in the conserve invariant

  Demo -- AI repair flow using ``valid_alternatives``:
    AI reads scenario A's anomaly, sees offending_op=tau.
    suggest_alternatives(tau) = (8, 10, 15) (['p', 'sigma', 'mobius'])
    AI picks 'p' (byte 0x08) and retries with (budget 3 (merge (p 3) (p 12))).
    New program retains the same structure, same cost -- still
    fails budget (same count of nodes), but AI's next step is to
    either raise budget (repair_hint says >= 4) or shrink body.

==============================================================================
  L3 -- static_analyze (pre-execution reasoning about programs)
==============================================================================

  pure integer computation
    program: (merge (p 12) (tau 100))
  nodes:           5
  max depth:       3
  effects:         {}
  budget bound:    <= 5 units
  deterministic:   True
  uses conserve:   False
  uses surprise:   False
  uses lineage:    False

  uses conservation budget
    program: (budget 100 (merge (p 12) (sigma 12)))
  nodes:           7
  max depth:       4
  effects:         {budget-scope}
  budget bound:    <= 7 units
  deterministic:   True
  uses conserve:   True
  uses surprise:   False
  uses lineage:    False

  uses surprise primitive
    program: (if-surprise (surprise 10 (p 12)) 999 0)
  nodes:           7
  max depth:       4
  effects:         {read-surprise, write-surprise-trace}
  budget bound:    <= 7 units
  deterministic:   True
  uses conserve:   False
  uses surprise:   True
  uses lineage:    False

  complex with let/ref
    program: (let 0 12 (merge (p (ref 0)) (sigma (ref 0))))
  nodes:           10
  max depth:       5
  effects:         {}
  budget bound:    <= 10 units
  deterministic:   True
  uses conserve:   False
  uses surprise:   False
  uses lineage:    False

  mixes conservation + surprise
    program: (conserve 77 (surprise 77 (p 12)))
  nodes:           6
  max depth:       4
  effects:         {conservation-check, write-surprise-trace}
  budget bound:    <= 6 units
  deterministic:   True
  uses conserve:   True
  uses surprise:   True
  uses lineage:    False

  interpretation:
    AI can ask 'what will this program do' without running it.
    The 'effects' set tells AI whether the program touches
    the surprise trace, a conservation scope, or is pure.
    'uses_surprise=True' is a flag that says 'this program
    interacts with the debugger primitive'.  AI can gate on
    that before executing in a sensitive context.

